The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (mi != NULL) {
    _ncesmp = mi->n_elts;
    _icetsm = mi->elt_id;
}
_volume_mass_injection_get_field_arrays(f->id, &_itpsmp, &_smcelp);
```
Reason:
The removal of braces around the conditional logic allowed `_volume_mass_injection_get_field_arrays(f->id, &_itpsmp, &_smcelp);` to execute even when `mi` was `NULL`. This could lead to accessing uninitialized data, resulting in a crash.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
_volume_mass_injection_get_field_arrays(f->id, &_itpsmp, &_smcelp);
if (_ncesmp > 0)
    _volume_mass_injection_get_field_arrays(CS_F_(p)->id, NULL, &_gamma);
```
Reason:
By ensuring that `_volume_mass_injection_get_field_arrays` is only called when `mi` is not `NULL` and `_ncesmp` is greater than zero, the patch prevents the function from executing under invalid conditions, thus avoiding potential crashes from uninitialized data access.

